!!! IMPORTANT - CDI4DC TOOL REQUIRES libncursesw5 AND MANY MODERN DISTROS DON'T SHIP IT - libncursesw6 IS FULLY BACKWARDS COMPATIBLE
YOU NEED TO MAKE THIS SYMLINK FOR IT TO WORK:

sudo ln -s /lib/i386-linux-gnu/libncurses.so.6 /lib/i386-linux-gnu/libncurses.so.5

Install instructions

Compiling from GNU/Linux:

Install one of these:
	genisofs OR mkisofs (When using mkisofs you need to uncomment the line starting with #mkisofs and comment the line starting with genisofs)

Install the KOS toolchain and run "source ./source_shell.sh"

To compile make sure you have 'make' installed and that kos-cc works.

To compile:
	'make'
	This makes a .elf that can be ran in a emulator like flycast - just drag it into the window.

To make a Dreamcast CD image for CD-ROM:
	'make format'
	This makes a compatible .iso and attempts to convert it to .cdi
	(!!! .ISO WONT WORK, IF CONVERTING TO CDI AUTOMATICALLY DOESNT WORK YOU NEED TO CONVERT IT BY YOURSELF !!!)
	You can drag and drop the .cdi to a emulator.

Editing the credentials:
	You can change the iplogo.png with your own image as long as it's 128 colors or less and is 320x90 or smaller.
	If it has transparent background - the color code for transparent is "#c0c0c0" or "192, 192, 192".
	It also must be under 8192 bytes.

	To edit the metadata edit the file ip.txt - the fields are self explainatory but don't edit what you don't understand.
	
https://dreamcast.wiki/Dreamcast.wiki for more info.
